Z||000000||MustangEater82||11-30-2001||07:18 PM||||I see you guys have had some talks about turboing 3.4L.  I am curious about some thing.  I am have a RWD GM 60 degree 3.4L in a 94 Camaro with a 5-speed.  What kind of internals are you guys using on your cars to get it going, also what kind of boost are you guys running?<P>What are you doing for hook up to turbo form exhaust, did you make custom manifolds.<P>Are you all using forged internals?<P>------------------<BR>1994 Medium Quaser Blue Camaro<BR>3.4L V6 w/ 5-speed<BR>Homeade CAI with a huge K&N cylinder filter, Single outlet Flowmaster with resonator, Accel 8mm ignition wires, Splitfire plugs, 3.42 gears and posi off a 97 WS6, 1 piece steel driveshaft, Converted to 4-wheel disc brakes<BR>Lightest Weight: 3160<BR>My fat ass: 260<BR>15.852@85.69<BR>Best R/T .511<BR>Best 60' 2.168<P>Father's Stock 2000 Navy Blue Camaro<BR>3.8L V6 w/ 5-speed<BR>15.875@88.25 With wheel spin in 1st<P>AIM: MustangEater82 <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||newfie||11-30-2001||09:30 PM||||I'm pretty sure the turbo's for the 2.8L fit the 3.4L(with fiero intake) engine also.  These turbo's are available at <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com</A> <BR>I don't know of any kits for the 3.4L camaro itself.  However I would rather custom make myself, need custom exhaust and intake made up as far as I know.  Get a used turbocharger from junkyard and rebuild or buy knew if you got the cash.  Do a bit of ECU reprogramming.  I personally think you should be able to turbo for under $1500.00 but then again I haven't actually done it yet so don't know potential problems.  I don't think you should run much over 10lbs boost without making the bottom end of your engine stonger.  Personally if I had a camaro I'd spend the extra $$ and drop in a V8. A fiero was made for a V6, a Camaro was made for a V8!  ||||reg||1
